      "content": "While it's possible that some swelling and warmth are related to normal inflammation, a larger calf difference may indicate an underlying issue. Elevating the leg and taking ibuprofen can help with swelling and pain, but it may not address the underlying cause. Considering your concerns, it's probably a good idea to contact your doctor, as they can assess your specific situation and provide guidance on managing the swelling and heat.",
